WEBVTT

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:21.850
Rhodonite!

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.370
Found you.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.490
<i>Asura Cryin' 2</i>

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.130
Do it, Misao-chan!

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.130
Okay!

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:30.890
Got it!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.300
Natsume-kun!

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.350
Didn't you know it would go right through her?

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.470
Sheesh, Tomo.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.550
How many plates have you broken so far?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.220
Maybe he's not suited to working at a pension.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.400
Looks like your kindness is going to waste, An-chan.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.310
A bed, meals...

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.130
...the beach, and girls in swimsuits.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.980
You get paid while enjoying a vacation.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.000
It should be a great job.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.380
Why you...

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.880
Look at them go.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.050
If only Kurosaki-senpai were here, too.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.720
It couldn't be helped.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.810
Shuri-san and Nia said they had some research to do.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.860
Don't move.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.870
"Free and Restricted Choices"

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.420
That's it, then?

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.360
You two are already like that?

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.090
Huh?

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.350
If you're dating, you should have said so.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.170
I've got plans too, you know.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.490
W-what? What kind of plans?

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.930
I can't say that here.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.950
Uh, um...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.540
I-it's almost time for my shift.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.740
I'll go get my apron.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.790
There she goes.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.550
I guess they aren't dating after all.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.080
Is that true, Tomo?

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.780
Come on! Don't look at me like that.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.370
Takatsuki and I aren't like that...

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.040
...and I'm not looking to date anyone right now.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:33.560
Besides, how am I supposed to date anyone with a ghost following me?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:34.970
So I'm a nuisance?

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.770
I see, I see.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.170
So you can't get a girlfriend...

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:43.410
...and you're a 16 year old virgin...

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.780
...because of me?

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:46.430
Well...

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.550
...it's not entirely your fault...

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.070
...but don't you think you have something to do with it?

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.040
Hello?

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.890
Hi Tomoharu.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:56.770
Shuri-san?

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.620
Having fun on your vacation?

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.380
I don't know about fun...

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.150
Misao-chan?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:04.730
What's wrong?

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:09.670
Is Sao-chan jealous because she caught you flirting with Kanade-chan?

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.100
Shuri-san, did you find what you were looking for?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.010
Yes.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.240
What are you looking for, anyway?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.390
Ruins.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.240
Ruins?

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:22.240
Yes.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.730
Ruins that might have something to do with releasing burial dolls.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.970
What? Where?

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.460
Why? Would you come help me if I told you?

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.900
Well, uh...

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:38.450
Shuri.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.600
Sorry. Gotta go, Tomoharu.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.360
Huh?

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.680
Wait, Shuri-san!

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:46.500
What'd she say?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.030
If she finds what she's looking for...

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.000
...maybe Kurosaki-senpai will meet us here.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.290
I don't think that'll happen.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.490
Shucks.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.930
That's too bad.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.460
Nia-chan is with her, right?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.160
Releasing burial dolls...

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.080
Be quick!

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.960
We'll leave as soon as everything's on board!

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:21.690
Kyomu-sama, we shouldn't be taking the Castas Machina Beta like this.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.100
Quiet!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.890
Don't question me.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:40.050
Just wait, Kagakagari.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:46.870
Delicious!

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.890
What a luxurious barbecue lunch!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.360
Now you'll have the energy to work this afternoon!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.530
Takatsuki, why don't you give that piece to Tomo?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.290
Thanks, Takatsuki.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.490
T-Takatsuki.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:06.840
It's hot.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:07.960
Be careful.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.520
Uh, sure.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.420
Huh? Where is Misao?

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.170
What are you doing over here?

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.050
Nothing.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.430
Don't worry.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.800
I won't stop you from seducing Takatsuki-san.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.830
I told you, that's not what I'm trying to do.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.500
Oh, really?

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.440
Look, if you have something to say, just say it!

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.750
I could tell you the same thing, Tomo.

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:56.370
Huh?

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:00.100
Tomo, you're hiding something from me, aren't you?

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.450
Huh? W-what?

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.040
Since Kagakagari's hijack incident...

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.360
...you've been acting weird.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.730
Did something happen after I went to sleep?

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.080
Not really, no.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:20.810
You know what happened.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.720
The plane landed safely...

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.950
...and no one was hurt.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.120
Nothing happened.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:36.820
Does Takatsuki-san know your secret?

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:46.370
So Takatsuki-san knows, but you can't tell me.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:52.800
Misao!

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.270
You jerk, Tomo!

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.000
You loser!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.150
Indecisive boob-obsessed freak!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.010
The meat was done so I brought you some.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:15.090
Did you have a fight?

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:18.090
It wasn't much of a fight.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:19.940
Misao just yelled at me.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.170
I see.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.380
Oh well.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.370
Well?

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:27.870
What do you want to do, Tomo?

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.190
What do I want to do?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.370
I'm asking if you don't want to date Takatsuki-san.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.570
Don't you think I have things to deal with...

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:39.980
...before I can even think about dating someone?

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.470
I could never have a normal relationship.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.960
Maybe you just feel guilty about Misao-chan.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:49.640
Huh?

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.430
You were both in that plane crash...

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.430
...but you were the one that survived.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.660
Maybe you feel bad about that.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.450
That's...

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.710
I wouldn't want that.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:05.360
I wouldn't want that to keep you from being happy.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:06.590
I think I'd be angry.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.390
Kyomu-sama, that's impossible!

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.530
There's nowhere to land!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.410
There isn't even space to set down the containers!

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.790
You're useless.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.380
Bismuth!

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.870
Kyomu-sama! You shouldn't do that here!

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:41.460
Quiet!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:42.980
Shut up and watch!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.250
Now you can land, right?

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.710
Well? What is this, Higuchi?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.180
Summer is about tests of courage.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:19.940
We'll pair up and go to that island.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.460
No, no, no. That's not what I meant.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:24.700
What this path here this afternoon?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:25.700
Nope.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.160
These rocks are only visible...

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:31.280
...when the tide goes out in the evening.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.890
How do you know that?

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.590
That island's famous among occult buffs.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.560
It's the remains of a battery constructed in the early Meiji period...

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.610
...the Kuremizaki fortress observatory.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:48.110
It's public cultural property...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.810
...but it's said that terrifying monsters are hiding under it.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:52.720
Wow!

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.160
But that's just a rumor.

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.710
Well, it's time for the Takatsuki and Tomoharu team to start.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.650
The next pair will go ten minutes after that.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.710
Takatsuki and I are a pair?

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.500
Why?

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.820
We're paired alphabetically.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.020
The Takatsuki and Natsume pair.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:10.580
What about you?

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:12.490
The Higuchi and Minakami pair.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:13.610
What about An?

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.930
She said she's tired and going to bed early.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.450
What?

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:23.390
What, you don't want to be paired with Takatsuki?

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.270
W-wait, that's not what I meant.

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:28.380
Well, that's that.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.440
Hurry up and go!

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:32.940
Excellent.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.670
Mission complete.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.400
What do you have planned, Higuchi?

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.570
Kuremizaki fortress observatory...

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.780
...also known as the lovers' battery.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:47.090
Visiting men and women are compelled to confess their hidden feelings...

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:50.710
...and become couples at this legendary island.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.350
That's stupid.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.640
Don't get in their way.

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:56.230
I won't!

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.060
Were you going to say something?

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:15.910
Um...

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.170
About the Asura Machina...

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:20.290
Huh?

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:24.610
Have you told Minakami-san...

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.810
...about the source of the Asura Machina's power?

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.540
I don't want to tell her if I can help it.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.860
At least, not until I can figure out how to release her from Kurogane.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.820
But to be honest...

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.110
...I don't know what I can do about that.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.690
You don't need to worry.

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:52.780
I'll protect you, Natsume-kun...

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.740
...in place of Minakami-san.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.650
I don't need a replacement for Misao.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:02.120
There's no need for you to put yourself in danger for me.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:06.760
I don't want to see you get hurt again.

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:09.340
I already made up my mind.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:10.050
Huh?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.370
I used to hate myself.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.920
My powers, my name.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.330
But you saved me, Natsume-kun.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.470
You saved me, Natsume-kun.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:24.970
Takatsuki...

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:34.580
This is my decision.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:52.410
Tomoharu?

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.900
Shuri-san? And Nia?

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.110
What are you two doing together?

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.010
W-what are you guys doing here?

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:08.210
These are the ruins we were looking for.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.030
Huh?

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.350
Then the key to releasing the burial dolls is here...

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.750
Shuri, this way.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.310
There's an entrance here.

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.330
I see.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:31.950
A secret door.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:36.440
At high tide, the key to the door is at the bottom of the ocean.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:41.580
That explains why we couldn't find an entrance above ground.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:43.200
Can you open it?

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.580
Of course!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.420
Right, her power to manipulate probability.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.100
I don't need that for a lock like this.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.090
Amazing.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:04.380
Maybe you forgot...

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.930
...Nia-chan's a child genius.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.570
Her clumsiness is on par with a genius', too.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:16.630
Aren't you going to go?

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:18.740
Misao.

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:45.380
Looks like someone was here before us.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.730
They're the Castas Machina that were guarding these ruins.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.230
Someone really did a number on them.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:53.760
But who?

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.220
It's the work of an Asura Cryin'!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.090
Let me start by introducing myself.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.920
My name is Kyomu Satomi...

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:10.260
...the man destined to reach the top of the Student Union.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.030
Don't forget it!

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.260
Looks like more trouble.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:17.370
Nia!

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.720
Did you say Asura Cryin'?

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.040
Is Kagakagari here?

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.480
Stay out of my way.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:29.180
I'm the one who'll kill Kagakagari.

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.210
So you met Kagakagari?

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:32.410
My sister...

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:34.410
Was my sister with him?

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:35.700
Nia-chan.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:43.340
You're the younger sister of Kagakagari's contracted demon Christina Fortuna.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.340
You look very similar.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.510
So you did meet my sister!

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:50.830
Why don't we exchange information?

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:52.510
Exchange information?

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:53.420
Yes.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.470
If you tell me what I want to know...

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:59.440
...I'll tell you what you want to know.

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.000
What do you want to know?

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.290
What is this place?

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.290
What are these ruins?

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:06.960
It's an Asura Machina testing facility.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.570
What? Really?

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.980
I wasn't convinced until I came inside...

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:13.980
...but I'm sure of it.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:17.740
There must be a device to release burial dolls here.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.500
Kagakagari came here for that.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.580
Now it's your turn, Kyomu Satomi.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.260
What are you talking about?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:32.720
You promised you'd tell me what you know about my sister!

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.980
Did I make a promise like that?

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:36.480
Why you...!

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.360
Bismuth.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:47.000
Nia!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:47.670
Nia-chan!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.550
Castas Machina?

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.900
You know too much.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.630
So you'll all die!

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:20.340
Just so you know, those aren't ordinary Castas Machina.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:25.860
They're a special version equipped with armor and anti-demon heavy arms.

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.180
Let go of me!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.210
I can't do that.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:33.700
You're going to be bait for Takaya Kagakagari.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.430
That jerk!

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:38.310
Tomo, call Kurogane!

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.110
Hurry!

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.020
Tomo?

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.100
Natsume-kun!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:44.070
Stand back!

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:50.590
Takatsuki, stop!

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:55.560
Takatsuki!

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.140
Is that all you can do?

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:00.580
How unfortunate.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.490
How about this?

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.810
From despair blacker than darkness...

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:09.890
What?

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:12.890
The fang that grieves the sin of science.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:20.730
Bismuth!

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.540
A spear that dispels magic?

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.820
Impressive, Shuri Kurosaki.

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.470
You surprise me.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:45.970
But I'm through here.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.290
Die.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:48.870
Die!

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.020
Oh, no!

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.310
Tomo, call Kurogane!

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:55.190
Tomo!

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:02.180
Shuri-san!

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:07.260
Why?

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:09.790
Why won't you call Kurogane?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.640
Say something, Tomo!

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:13.700
Tomoharu!

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:16.130
Take Kanade and run!

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.190
Go, Tomoharu!

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.860
Hurry up and die!

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:47.830
Brother...

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:21.270
Alone.

00:23:21.530 --> 00:23:22.440
Not alone.

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:23.740
Mass of the future.

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.000
Width of the past.

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:26.530
Cast into a cloud of dust.
